<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23339" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ingauni</span></b> , ōrum,
		m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				people of Liguria</i>, <i>on the sea - coast</i>,
				<i>at the foot of the Maritime Alps</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 28,
			46</span></i>; <i><span class="en">30,
			19</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Album
				Ingaunum</span></b> , <i>their capital city</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 3, 9, 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5, 7, § 48</span></i>;
			called also: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Albingaunum</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 2,
			15</span></i>; its inhabitants are called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Albingauni Lĭ-gŭres</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Liv. 29, 5,
				2</span></i>.</div>
